cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Sabline capability format, please cite this repository
  as below. A preprint describing Sabline and this format is
  forthcoming; until it is published, this entry is the citation.
title: "sabline-spec: the Sabline capability format"
abstract: >-
  A specification of the effects a Sabline program may declare, the
  grammar an operator uses to grant them, what a runtime must refuse,
  the sabline.audit/1, sabline.capabilities/1 and sabline.receipt/1 JSON
  documents, in-toto predicate types for the audit and for the receipt of
  a run, and a language-independent
  conformance corpus at three levels. Its reference implementation is
  sabline-lang.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Palakurthi
    given-names: Gowri Shankar
repository-code: "https://github.com/gowrishankar-infra/sabline-spec"
license: CC0-1.0
version: "0.14.0"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
keywords:
  - specification
  - effect system
  - capabilities
  - conformance
  - in-toto
references:
